= The SNP Moves Against Callaghan

Callaghan has refused to bring the repeal order to an early vote and is offering talks instead. The SNP has had enough. Its MPs have tabled a motion of no confidence in the government.

The Liberals say they will vote against the government. The Ulster Unionists are divided, and Plaid Cymru is being bought off with compensation for slate quarrymen. Whitelaw thinks a Conservative motion would attract more votes than the SNP's. It could come down to a single vote.

- @no_confidence.vote: Table a Conservative motion of no confidence.
- @wait: Wait for the autumn and an election on Callaghan's terms.

@wait
on-arrival: dry_dissent += 5; right_dissent += 5; thatcher_rating -= 2

We let the moment pass. The government limps on, and the election will come in the autumn.
